    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Bilal</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">Prayer times, the mushaf, athkar and the Qibla. No account, no ads, and nothing about you leaves this phone unless you turn it on. Change the language any time in Settings.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_location_title">Where you are</string>
    <string name="onboarding_location_body">Prayer times and the Qibla are worked out for your position, on this phone. Location is used only while the app is open, never in the background. You can choose a city by hand instead.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_alerts_title">Alerts that arrive</string>
    <string name="onboarding_alerts_body">Android needs your permission to show prayer alerts, and a second one to deliver them on the minute rather than whenever it suits. If alerts still come late, Settings has a screen that shows exactly what on your phone is stopping them.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_smart_title">Reacting to the day</string>
    <string name="onboarding_smart_body">Bilal notices Jumu\'ah, Ramadan\'s nights, Arafah and the rest of the Islamic year, and offers the dua for the weather outside. Weather sends your location, rounded to about a kilometre, to Open-Meteo once an hour while the app is open. Turn it off in Settings whenever you like.</string>
